  "body": "**Stacked on #957** (issue #852, `issue/852-necked-tool-envelope`): this branch was cut from #957's head because both change `crates/app/src/sim_tool_body.rs`. Until #957 merges, this PR's diff also shows #957's commit (`54ed3fe7`); the #1038 change is the single commit on top (`feat(sim): draw a turning tool's lathe body at the tool position`). Retarget/merge order per AGENTS.md \"Overlapping issues stack\".\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0 (PROCESS_VERSION 16).\n\n## What changed\n\nBefore, `sim_tool_body::for_operation` returned `Ok(None)` for every lathe-held kind, so the simulation and viewport showed only the axis marker for a turning tool, whatever body it carried. Now:\n\n- **New `app::sim_lathe_body`.** It holds a pure pose (`posed(facets, tip, &LatheAxes)`), which maps a tool-frame point (x, y, z) to `tip + x*radial + y*(z x x) + z*along`, and a `LatheBodyCache`. The cache fetches the op's tool's lathe-frame body (`ToolBody::facets`, the same mesh `LatheClearance` is derived from) together with the frame it is judged in. It refits that frame only when the op, its path signature or the body (by `Arc` identity) changes, so the fit does not run every frame.\n- **The frame is the holder law's own.** `operation::lathe_body_axes` (= `turning_holder::body_axes`) runs `Frame::about` on the op's source facets (`source_facets`, the read the law and the lathe stock sim use) and takes the radial from `SignedMeridian::of` on the cached path (a new `SignedMeridian::axes` accessor). As a result, every drawn vertex sits where the law reads it: sqrt((X + x)^2 + y^2) from the axis, at station S + z.\n- **`SimToolCache::posed`** tries the lathe arm first. The ui seam (`world::sim_tool_tris`) is unchanged, so this adds no second drawing path. `for_operation` now also returns `Ok(None)` for a tool that carries a lathe-frame body, which covers a `Bore` with a lathe body: it is drawn as that body, not as the revolved bar stand-in.\n- **A turning tool without a lathe body draws as before** (axis marker only). If the frame cannot be fitted, the refusal is logged once by name and nothing is drawn. No pose is guessed.\n- **Display only.** No verdict, warning or posted output changes.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/1038-lathe-body-in-sim.md`.\n\n## Tests\n\nPinned by the new `crates/app/tests/sim_lathe_body.rs`:\n- `an_od_holder_is_drawn_at_the_tip_radially_out_up_the_spindle`: OD finish ride with an OD shank, checked at several moves. Every drawn vertex equals its tool-frame vertex posed at the tip (+x along the path radial, +z up the spindle), matches the law's radius identity, and gives one drawn facet per body facet (not revolved).\n- `an_id_bar_is_drawn_toward_the_axis_up_the_bore`: boring ride with a slim bar. Same vertex-by-vertex check; the bar stands inside the tip radius, its near corners at hypot(X - 4, 1.5), and it runs up the bore.\n- `a_turning_tool_without_a_lathe_body_draws_as_before`: the bare insert draws nothing and the cache stays empty with no refusal.\n- `a_new_body_is_drawn_at_once_and_the_frame_freed_with_the_transport`: reuse, rebuild on a new body, freed on `clear`.\n- `the_pose_maps_each_tool_axis_onto_its_world_direction`: the pure pose on explicit axes, plus refusal of zero, non-finite and skew frames.\n\nAlso run: `sim_tool_body`, `tool_neck_laws`, `turning_holder`, `turning_insert_zone` and `tool_body` (all green), the full `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on the final head, and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No live GUI check: nobody has stepped a turning op in the running app to look at the drawn body. The ui call path is unchanged and is covered by the existing `tool_body` ui test for milling only.\n- Tinting the body on a `HolderHit` move (the issue's optional \"could\") is not done. It needs a colour channel on the sim body part; see the decision file.\n- No snapshot PNG changed.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Simulation and viewport draw a turning tool's imported lathe holder body at the tool position, posed in the frame the holder law judges it in (OD and ID), instead of only the axis marker (#1038)\n\nFixes #1038\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
